The graph shows the average amount of rainfall in July for each region of the country, with the bars representing the amount of rainfall for each region. If the average amount of rainfall for the entire country in July is 35.2 mm, and the North and South regions receive a total of 1200 mm of rainfall, what is the average amount of rainfall for the remaining three regions?

[asy]
size(300);
defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(6pt));

int[] rainfall={65,50,32,42,27};
int[] regions={North,South,East,West,Central};

path unitbox=(0,0)--(0,1)--(1,1)--(1,0);

for(int i = 0; i < 5; ++i)
{
transform region=shift(5+20*i,0)*scale(5,rainfall[i]);
fill(region*unitbox,gray);
draw(region*unitbox);
label(Label(string(rainfall[i])), (7.5+20*i, rainfall[i]), N);
label(Label(format("%s", regions[i])), (10+20*i, 0), S);
}

xaxis(xmin=0, xmax=100, above=true);
yaxis(ymin=0, ymax=80, Ticks(Step=10, begin=false, beginlabel=false, step=10, Size=3), above=true);

label(rotate(90)*"Rainfall (mm)", (-15,40), fontsize(8pt));

label("Average Rainfall in July for Each Region", (50,90), fontsize(10pt));
label("(Entire Country Average: 35.2 mm)", (50, 85), fontsize(8pt));

[/asy]
